<title>UK: European cotton buying stifled by strong dollar.</title>
<headline>European cotton buying stifled by strong dollar.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prices for raw cotton in Europe were quoted unchanged since Friday but buyers were not tempted, market sources said.</p>
<p>The strength of the US dollar was generally held to be responsible, discouraging buyers from placing firm orders, they said.</p>
<p>Despite evidence that millers in some markets were short of cover for nearby requirements, there was little active buying seen.</p>
<p>-London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
